    <Placemark>
      <name>Lincoln and Districts Community Care </name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: A not for profit charitable organisation (charity number CC 30052) that provides and coordinates health and social services for those in need in the across Selwyn communities. We work collaboratively with other organisations to ensure residents' needs are met. Pegasus Health Community worker: supports people across Selwyn to access the health services they are entitled to. Works with local GPs and Practice Nurses throughout Selwyn. Senior Exercise programme: twice weekly on Monday and Thursday from 10-11am at Lincoln University Recreation Centre. Tutored by a professional Gym Instructor and for a moderate annual membership fee. Lincoln Walking groups: Tuesday and Wednesday. Lead the Way: free mentoring service - teaching families various skills to enable self sufficiency. Volunteers  transport people to appointments for those who cannot drive (including into the city). Referrals to home handymen and other services and supports such as counselling and budgeting services. Free education sessions and groups for international people to help adjust to our New Zealand lifestyle e.g. conversational English. <br>Contact person: Janet Saunders<br>phone number: 325-2007<br>email: servicesdevelopment@lincolncomcare.co.nz<br>website (or Fb): ,http://facebook.com/lincolncommunitycare  http://www.lincolncomcare.co.nz<br>Address: 16 Lyttelton Street, Lincoln 7608<br>Subject: Budgets, Personal, Meals on wheels programmes, Community groups, Cultural groups, Educational groups, Health and welfare, Older people -- Medical care, Welfare, Counselling, Home and family, Languages, Exercise for older people<br>Last update: 12/6/2018<br>X latitude: -43.639639<br>Y longitude: 172.4823884]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Description">
          <value><![CDATA[A not for profit charitable organisation (charity number CC 30052) that provides and coordinates health and social services for those in need in the across Selwyn communities. We work collaboratively with other organisations to ensure residents' needs are met. Pegasus Health Community worker: supports people across Selwyn to access the health services they are entitled to. Works with local GPs and Practice Nurses throughout Selwyn. Senior Exercise programme: twice weekly on Monday and Thursday from 10-11am at Lincoln University Recreation Centre. Tutored by a professional Gym Instructor and for a moderate annual membership fee. Lincoln Walking groups: Tuesday and Wednesday. Lead the Way: free mentoring service - teaching families various skills to enable self sufficiency. Volunteers  transport people to appointments for those who cannot drive (including into the city). Referrals to home handymen and other services and supports such as counselling and budgeting services. Free education sessions and groups for international people to help adjust to our New Zealand lifestyle e.g. conversational English. ]]></value>
        </Data>
