    <Placemark>
      <name>Ashley-Rakahuri Rivercare Group</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: The major objective of the group is to improve the breeding success of native birds which nest in the Ashley/Rakahuri riverbed. The focus is on three endangered native species - the wrybill plover, the black-fronted tern and the black-billed gull. The river is the northernmost breeding site for the wrybill, the only bird in the world with a bill which turns sideways. Meetings are held 4-5 times annually, not at set times. Most group activity takes place on and around the river just before and during the breeding season (August-January). We have also helped in the construction of walkways, 4WD tracks and swimming holes, in order to attract recreational users of the riverbed away from the core breeding sites. <br>Contact person: NIck Ledgard<br>phone number: 03 313-8382<br>email: nick.ledgard@xtra.co.nz<br>website (or Fb): http://www.facebook.com/ashleyrivercare , http://www.ashleyrivercare.org.nz<br>Address: 191 Carrs Road, RD2 Rangiora 7472<br>Subject: Birds, Conservation of natural resources, Rivers, Community groups<br>Last update: 11/7/2018<br>X latitude: -43.251186<br>Y longitude: 172.559187]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Description">
          <value>The major objective of the group is to improve the breeding success of native birds which nest in the Ashley/Rakahuri riverbed. The focus is on three endangered native species - the wrybill plover, the black-fronted tern and the black-billed gull. The river is the northernmost breeding site for the wrybill, the only bird in the world with a bill which turns sideways. Meetings are held 4-5 times annually, not at set times. Most group activity takes place on and around the river just before and during the breeding season (August-January). We have also helped in the construction of walkways, 4WD tracks and swimming holes, in order to attract recreational users of the riverbed away from the core breeding sites. </value>
        </Data>
        <Data name="Contact person">
          <value>NIck Ledgard</value>
        </Data>
