    <Placemark>
      <name>Christchurch Guangdong Association</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: 1. To maintain and promote Cantonese (Guangdong) culture and traditions in New Zealand, 2. To contribute to the formation and success of a multi-cultural environment in New Zealand, 3. To provide opportunities for communication, interaction, recreation and mutual support amongst all Cantonese (Guangdong) Chinese in New Zealand, 4. To help Cantonese (Guangdong) immigrants adapt to New Zealand and provide a support base for newly arrived Cantonese (Guangdong) Chinese immigrants and visitors to New Zealand, 5. To publish newsletters regularly to inform Association members of community news and activities, 6. To organize and participate in social activities beneficial to New Zealand society and to contribute to the economic and social development of New Zealand, 7. To facilitate interaction and cooperation between Chinese communities and other ethnic communities in New Zealand, 8. Subject to the provisions of the Friendly Societies and Credit Unions Act 1982, to acquire and own assets and to invest the funds of the Association to enable the Association to operate effectively, 9. To employ people for the administration of the Association. 10. To be and to remain non-political and non-religious<br>Contact person: Don Yee<br>phone number: 377-2827<br>email: donyee888@xtra.co.nz<br>website (or Fb): http://www.cgda.org.nz/<br>Address: L Block, 31 Vicki Street, Sockburn, Christchurch 8042<br>Subject: Immigrants, Community groups, Ethnic groups, Chinese, Cultural groups, Languages, Chinese language<br>Last update: 11/22/2018<br>X latitude: -43.53563<br>Y longitude: 172.56669]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Description">
          <value>1. To maintain and promote Cantonese (Guangdong) culture and traditions in New Zealand, 2. To contribute to the formation and success of a multi-cultural environment in New Zealand, 3. To provide opportunities for communication, interaction, recreation and mutual support amongst all Cantonese (Guangdong) Chinese in New Zealand, 4. To help Cantonese (Guangdong) immigrants adapt to New Zealand and provide a support base for newly arrived Cantonese (Guangdong) Chinese immigrants and visitors to New Zealand, 5. To publish newsletters regularly to inform Association members of community news and activities, 6. To organize and participate in social activities beneficial to New Zealand society and to contribute to the economic and social development of New Zealand, 7. To facilitate interaction and cooperation between Chinese communities and other ethnic communities in New Zealand, 8. Subject to the provisions of the Friendly Societies and Credit Unions Act 1982, to acquire and own assets and to invest the funds of the Association to enable the Association to operate effectively, 9. To employ people for the administration of the Association. 10. To be and to remain non-political and non-religious</value>
        </Data>
