    <Placemark>
      <name>Christchurch City Libraries. Learning Centres</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: Te HÄpua: Halswell Centre. The Learning Centres are technology-rich education resource centres which aim to extend horizons and develop confident, creative and collaborative learners through a dynamic technological environment. They provide programmes for all learners from preschool to older adult. The programmes are designed to support and help customers develop the skills they may need to make better use of new technologies to improve their access to and use of information. Programmes also support teachers, families and students in their literacy and numeracy  education. Examples include digital photography, family history research, CV writing, newsletter creation, beginner computer sessions, introduction to iPads, using online auctions, using Google and learning to research more cleverly, computer animation and graphics, creative writing and digital stories, movie making and school holiday programmes. Special programmes can be developed with schools and community groups to support specific learning goals or requirements. <br>Contact person: <br>phone number: 941-5140<br>email: learningcentre@ccc.govt.nz<br>website (or Fb): http://christchurchcitylibraries.com/LearningCentres/Community/Holidays/"<br>Address:  341 Halswell Road, Halswell<br>Subject: Digital cameras, Motion pictures, Photography -- Digital techniques, Computers and older people, Internet and older people, Citizen and consumer, Libraries, Public libraries, Community groups, Educational groups, Books and reading, Computer-assisted instruction, Educational acceleration, Information technology, Internet in education, Learning, Literacy programmes, Multimedia systems, After-school programmes, RÃ©sumÃ©s (Employment), Personal development, Creative writing, Employment re-entry, Internet, Internet auctions, Mathematics, Computers, Computer animation, Computer graphics, Electronic mail systems, Microsoft PowerPoint (Computer file), Three-dimensional display systems, Virtual reality, Word processing<br>Last update: 11/21/2018<br>X latitude: -43.581229<br>Y longitude: 172.568931]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Description">
          <value>Te HÄpua: Halswell Centre. The Learning Centres are technology-rich education resource centres which aim to extend horizons and develop confident, creative and collaborative learners through a dynamic technological environment. They provide programmes for all learners from preschool to older adult. The programmes are designed to support and help customers develop the skills they may need to make better use of new technologies to improve their access to and use of information. Programmes also support teachers, families and students in their literacy and numeracy  education. Examples include digital photography, family history research, CV writing, newsletter creation, beginner computer sessions, introduction to iPads, using online auctions, using Google and learning to research more cleverly, computer animation and graphics, creative writing and digital stories, movie making and school holiday programmes. Special programmes can be developed with schools and community groups to support specific learning goals or requirements. </value>
        </Data>
