    <Placemark>
      <name>Christian Arabic Fellowship</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: Community based trust committed to show in practical ways the love of the Lord and the love of one another by providing values and resources to the Arabic Community members in Canterbury regardless of age, religion, gender or race. Offers practical help and support to new migrants so that they can establish themselves in New Zealand. Serving the Arabic Community through the media like Radio and TV production. This is to keep the ethnic group of the Arabic Community connected to their culture, music and their special events and to inform them about the new rules and regulations in our new home country New Zealand. Organises outdoor activities to our Arabic Community members so that they can feel the unity of their ethnic group and background. Weekly radio programme every Sunday night from 7 to 8 p.m on PLAINS FM 96.9. Weekly spiritual meetings<br>Contact person: Mosa Bekheet<br>phone number: 322-6470<br>email: mosa@clear.net.nz<br>website (or Fb): https://www.facebook.com/pg/Arabic-Christian-Fellowship-739043259548204/about/?ref=page_internal<br>Address: St. Margaret's Presbyterian Church, Cnr Farrington Avenue & Kilburn Street, Christchurch, 8053<br>Subject: Community groups, Church groups, Ethnic groups, Arabic speaking people<br>Last update: 11/22/2018<br>X latitude: -43.4930381<br>Y longitude: 172.5879793]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Description">
          <value>Community based trust committed to show in practical ways the love of the Lord and the love of one another by providing values and resources to the Arabic Community members in Canterbury regardless of age, religion, gender or race. Offers practical help and support to new migrants so that they can establish themselves in New Zealand. Serving the Arabic Community through the media like Radio and TV production. This is to keep the ethnic group of the Arabic Community connected to their culture, music and their special events and to inform them about the new rules and regulations in our new home country New Zealand. Organises outdoor activities to our Arabic Community members so that they can feel the unity of their ethnic group and background. Weekly radio programme every Sunday night from 7 to 8 p.m on PLAINS FM 96.9. Weekly spiritual meetings</value>
        </Data>
        <Data name="Contact person">
          <value>Mosa Bekheet</value>
        </Data>
        <Data name="phone number">
          <value>322-6470</value>
        </Data>
        <Data name="email">
          <value>mosa@clear.net.nz</value>
        </Data>
        <Data name="website (or Fb)">
          <value>https://www.facebook.com/pg/Arabic-Christian-Fellowship-739043259548204/about/?ref=page_internal</value>
        </Data>
        <Data name="Address">
          <value><![CDATA[St. Margaret's Presbyterian Church, Cnr Farrington Avenue & Kilburn Street, Christchurch, 8053]]></value>
        </Data>
        <Data name="Subject">
          <value>Community groups, Church groups, Ethnic groups, Arabic speaking people</value>
