    <Placemark>
      <name>National Council of Women. Christchurch Branch</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: The National Council of Women of New Zealand (NCWNZ) is the country's leading women's organisation. We work to promote women's rights and equality. NCWNZ branches are particularly active in the community and hold monthly meetings to discuss current issues and arrange branch initiatives. Branch initiatives range from engaging expert speakers to provide informative talks, to lobbying officials, or hosting events, such as suffrage celebrations. Branches also engage with local bodies to formulate community policy, as well as provide support to other community organisations<br>Contact person: Penny Devine<br>phone number: 027-274-2444<br>email: ncwnzchristchurch@gmail.com<br>website (or Fb): http://www.ncwnz.org.nz<br>Address: 8 Tui Street, Fendalton, Christchurch 8042<br>Subject: Citizen and consumer, Community groups, Women -- Societies and clubs, Women -- Education<br>Last update: 12/12/2018<br>X latitude: -43.51951467<br>Y longitude: 172.5974075]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Description">
          <value><![CDATA[The National Council of Women of New Zealand (NCWNZ) is the country's leading women's organisation. We work to promote women's rights and equality. NCWNZ branches are particularly active in the community and hold monthly meetings to discuss current issues and arrange branch initiatives. Branch initiatives range from engaging expert speakers to provide informative talks, to lobbying officials, or hosting events, such as suffrage celebrations. Branches also engage with local bodies to formulate community policy, as well as provide support to other community organisations]]></value>
