    <Placemark>
      <name>Christchurch Folk Music Club</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: We vary our concerts and encourage local performers along, as well as regularly hosting international visiting artists and groups. This level of diversity brings to our audiences a broad range of musical experience, in addition to the myriad educational opportunities inherent in cultural exchange.  The Folk Club acknowledges the role of music as one of the most popular forms of leisure and relaxation across all realms of our society  given its broad appeal and the potential to break through language,  generational and cultural barriers. We aim to provide both a safe place to start performing in the public arena and an equally attractive platform for the more sophisticated performers to showcase their work. The Club sees one of its major roles as that of a catalyst for musicians to further develop their performance skills<br>Contact person: Judi Smitheram<br>phone number: 274,543,885<br>email: secretary@folkmusic.org.nz<br>website (or Fb): http://www.facebook.com/pages/Christchurch-Folk-Music-Club/132568930133787 http://www.folkmusic.org.nz/<br>Address: 29 Domain Terrace, Spreydon, Christchurch 8024<br>Subject: Arts, crafts and hobbies, Community groups, Cultural groups, Music, Folk music, Educational groups, Home and family, Personal development<br>Last update: 11/22/2018<br>X latitude: -43.5573354<br>Y longitude: 172.603538]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Description">
          <value>We vary our concerts and encourage local performers along, as well as regularly hosting international visiting artists and groups. This level of diversity brings to our audiences a broad range of musical experience, in addition to the myriad educational opportunities inherent in cultural exchange.  The Folk Club acknowledges the role of music as one of the most popular forms of leisure and relaxation across all realms of our society  given its broad appeal and the potential to break through language,  generational and cultural barriers. We aim to provide both a safe place to start performing in the public arena and an equally attractive platform for the more sophisticated performers to showcase their work. The Club sees one of its major roles as that of a catalyst for musicians to further develop their performance skills</value>
        </Data>
        <Data name="Contact person">
          <value>Judi Smitheram</value>
        </Data>
        <Data name="phone number">
          <value>274,543,885</value>
        </Data>
        <Data name="email">
          <value>secretary@folkmusic.org.nz</value>
        </Data>
        <Data name="website (or Fb)">
          <value>http://www.facebook.com/pages/Christchurch-Folk-Music-Club/132568930133787 http://www.folkmusic.org.nz/</value>
        </Data>
