    <Placemark>
      <name>Ryder Cheshire Foundation. Canterbury</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: Ryder Cheshire Foundation is a not for profit charitable organisation. In keeping with the vision of our founders, Group Captain Lord Leonard Cheshire of Woodhall and Baroness Ryder of Warsaw, we are dedicated to alleviate human suffering by providing relief and rehabilitation facilities to those in need and to be a model centre of excellence in the chosen fields.  Ryder Cheshire Homes are in New Zealand, Australia, East Timor and  India. These homes have medical residential and day clinics and some  include  services for people with TB and  a day school for children with disabilities. Teachers, physiotherapists, medical professionals and people who can make a difference to the residents  are welcome, as volunteers. In India and east Timor there is a mess for the volunteers and food is provided at a moderate charge. Volunteers with various skills come from many countries stay for 3 months to 1 year. For further information regarding an application for a volunteer, annual membership of $25 and information regarding sponsoring a child please contact our Treasurer or Chairperson.<br>Contact person: Carolyn Tapley<br>phone number: 355-4713<br>email: carolyn.tapley@broadbase.co.nz<br>website (or Fb): http://www.rydercheshire.co.nz/<br>Address: 129 Glandovey Road, Strowan, Christchurch 8052<br>Subject: Community groups, Fund raising, Overseas aid<br>Last update: 12/20/2018<br>X latitude: -43.5134226<br>Y longitude: 172.6075635]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Description">
          <value>Ryder Cheshire Foundation is a not for profit charitable organisation. In keeping with the vision of our founders, Group Captain Lord Leonard Cheshire of Woodhall and Baroness Ryder of Warsaw, we are dedicated to alleviate human suffering by providing relief and rehabilitation facilities to those in need and to be a model centre of excellence in the chosen fields.  Ryder Cheshire Homes are in New Zealand, Australia, East Timor and  India. These homes have medical residential and day clinics and some  include  services for people with TB and  a day school for children with disabilities. Teachers, physiotherapists, medical professionals and people who can make a difference to the residents  are welcome, as volunteers. In India and east Timor there is a mess for the volunteers and food is provided at a moderate charge. Volunteers with various skills come from many countries stay for 3 months to 1 year. For further information regarding an application for a volunteer, annual membership of $25 and information regarding sponsoring a child please contact our Treasurer or Chairperson.</value>
        </Data>
        <Data name="Contact person">
          <value>Carolyn Tapley</value>
        </Data>
        <Data name="phone number">
          <value>355-4713</value>
        </Data>
        <Data name="email">
          <value>carolyn.tapley@broadbase.co.nz</value>
        </Data>
