    <Placemark>
      <name>Cancer Society of New Zealand. Canterbury West Coast Division. Accommodation Services</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: Provides accommodation, companionship and support for cancer patients and caregivers who are facing extended time away from the comfort and surroundings of their own home. Also available for day patients. Your treatment centre can arrange accommodation at your request. Referrals from other health professionals, Cancer Society staff and self referrals are also accepted. If eligible, a claim will be made on your behalf for a government subsidy. Quality Christchurch accommodation: family rooms, cooking facilities, communal lounges, limited off street parking, access to a laundry, support from Cancer Society staff, transport to appointments, access to the Internet. <br>Contact person: Hannah Adair<br>phone number: 0800 226-237 (Cancer Information Service) , 379-5835<br>email: daffodil.reception@cancercwc.org.nz<br>website (or Fb): http://www.facebook.com/cancercwc , http://www.twitter.com/cancercwc , http://www.cancernz.org.nz/divisions/canterbury-westcoast/about/<br>Address: 91 Papanui Road, Merivale, Christchurch 8014<br>Subject: Community groups, Health and welfare, Cancer -- Patients -- Housing<br>Last update: 11/14/2018<br>X latitude: -43.5169732<br>Y longitude: 172.6245682]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Description">
          <value>Provides accommodation, companionship and support for cancer patients and caregivers who are facing extended time away from the comfort and surroundings of their own home. Also available for day patients. Your treatment centre can arrange accommodation at your request. Referrals from other health professionals, Cancer Society staff and self referrals are also accepted. If eligible, a claim will be made on your behalf for a government subsidy. Quality Christchurch accommodation: family rooms, cooking facilities, communal lounges, limited off street parking, access to a laundry, support from Cancer Society staff, transport to appointments, access to the Internet. </value>
        </Data>
        <Data name="Contact person">
