      <name>Christchurch South Community Gardens Trust </name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: Community Garden in Sydenham. Established 1999. Learn about gardening practices, composting, recycling and provide food for the community. All welcome to help in the garden or donate / koha for plants and produce.  Research students invited and school programmes available to enhance the curriculum. Expressions of interest to join the board of trustees always welcome - please supply a brief biography<br>Contact person: Christine Blance<br>phone number: 942-6630<br>email: info@cscommunitygardens.net.nz<br>website (or Fb): http://www.cscommunitygardens.net.nz<br>Address: 188 Strickland Street, Spreydon, Christchurch 8024<br>Subject: Arts, crafts and hobbies, Gardening, Community gardens, Citizen and consumer, Community groups, Educational groups, Homeless persons -- Food, Home and family, Occupational training, Sports and recreation<br>Last update: 11/22/2018<br>X latitude: -43.5498778<br>Y longitude: 172.6286522]]></description>
