    <Placemark>
      <name>Unitarian Universalist Fellowship of Christchurch</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: We unite in the tradition of a liberal religious community, coming together to develop individually through worship, the arts, fellowship and service. We have no dogma, but believe that truth is to be found through the open and free exchange of ideas. Our roots are Christian, but we find inspiration in all world religions, science and our own reasoning. We strive to live ethically and in harmony within the world and to pursue the vision of peace, liberty and justice<br>Contact person: Derek McCullough<br>phone number: 021-752-695 <br>email: <br>website (or Fb): http://www.uuchristchurch.org<br>Address: WEA, 59 Gloucester Street, Christchurch Central, Christchurch 8013<br>Subject: Community groups, Unitarianism, Church groups<br>Last update: 1/9/2019<br>X latitude: -43.52969646<br>Y longitude: 172.631611]]></description>
