      <description><![CDATA[Description: Anglican churches. Traditional and contemporary worship opportunities. We have a range of activities for the community. Churches available for weddings taken by Vicar Joanne Latham, assistant minister or other ministers of religion by negotiation. Funerals taken by Vicar or assistant minister or licensed Anglican Minister. St Silas: hall, lounge, foyer area, well equipped kitchen, available for hire for community groups and functions. Private functions by negotiation. St. Silas and St. David's, Badminton, Gentle exercise group, Table tennis, Indoor Bowls, Old Time Dance Group, Music and movement for parents, caregivers and preschoolers, Ballet - Adair Botting School of Dance, Youth group for years 6-8, Senior group for years 9-13.<br>Contact person: Colin Eaton<br>phone number: 352-1366<br>email: davidandsilas@xtra.co.nz<br>website (or Fb): http://www.davidandsilas.org.nz<br>Address: 827 Main North Road, Belfast, Christchurch 8051<br>Subject: Halls, meeting rooms, etc., Community groups, Church groups, Anglican Church in Aotearoa New Zealand and Polynesia, Church work with children, Play groups -- Music, After-school programmes, People with disabilities -- Services for, Physical fitness, Church work with youth, Marriage counselling, Bible -- Study and teaching, Badminton (Game), Table tennis, Physical fitness<br>Last update: 11/1/2018<br>X latitude: -43.4429398<br>Y longitude: 172.6337256]]></description>
