    <Placemark>
      <name>Victim Support. Christchurch</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: Victim Support offers 24-hour support for people affected by crime or trauma. Here's how we can help: provide immediate support in a crisis, give you information, advise you on your rights, listen and talk, refer you to counselling, assist and support you at court trials and hearings, give you help to access other specialist support services. Provide emergency grants and financial assistance to help you deal with or recover from your experience, prepare victim impact statements and attend family group or restorative justice conferences. Help you regain control and rebuild your life<br>Contact person: Demelza Faimalo<br>phone number: 0800 VICTIM<br>email: nationaloffice@victimsupport.org.nz<br>website (or Fb): http://facebook.com/VictimSupportNZ  http://www.victimsupport.org.nz/<br>Address: 40 Lichfield Street, Christchurch Central, Christchurch 8011<br>Subject: Community groups, Health and welfare, Homelessness, Homeless persons -- Services for, Sexual abuse victims -- Services for, Counselling, Victims, Victims -- Services for<br>Last update: 1/9/2019<br>X latitude: -43.5343942<br>Y longitude: 172.6351869]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Description">
          <value><![CDATA[Victim Support offers 24-hour support for people affected by crime or trauma. Here's how we can help: provide immediate support in a crisis, give you information, advise you on your rights, listen and talk, refer you to counselling, assist and support you at court trials and hearings, give you help to access other specialist support services. Provide emergency grants and financial assistance to help you deal with or recover from your experience, prepare victim impact statements and attend family group or restorative justice conferences. Help you regain control and rebuild your life]]></value>
        </Data>
        <Data name="Contact person">
