    <Placemark>
      <name>Canterbury Business Association</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: Supports immigrant job seekers with a mentoring programme, and supports Christchurch ethical businesses. Our organisations are interested in social enterprise, community development, and international connectedness of Christchurch to the rest of the world. We are particularly interested in emerging economies where a growing number of our immigrants to Christchurch, who help with the rebuild, come from. We work collaboratively with migrant and ethnic communities and the wider community. We consult widely on a range of issues including infrastructure development, and business development with expertise found within the Association<br>Contact person: Taz Mukorombindo<br>phone number: 379-4222<br>email: contact@canterburybusiness.org.nz<br>website (or Fb): http://www.canterburybusiness.org.nz<br>Address: 166 St Asaph Street, Christchurch Central, Christchurch 8011<br>Subject: Citizen and consumer, Immigrants -- Employment, Refugees -- Employment, Community groups, Ethnic groups, Business -- Societies, etc., Cultural groups, Occupational training, Personal development, Immigrants -- Services for, Refugees -- Services for<br>Last update: 11/14/2018<br>X latitude: -43.5366896<br>Y longitude: 172.6353423]]></description>
