    <Placemark>
      <name>Life in Vacant Spaces</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: Life in Vacant Spaces (LIVS) brokers and activates otherwise vacant property for public and private landowners in order to find short and medium-term uses for the vacant sites and buildings of our city. LIVS inspires local people to activate the cityâ€™s vacant areas with creative, intriguing and entrepreneurial projects. LIVS does not own properties or permanently develop sites, but rather coordinates complementary and evolving temporary uses until a future long term activity takes place<br>Contact person: Rachael Welfare <br>phone number: info@livs.org.nz<br>email: <br>website (or Fb): <br>Address: 193 St Asaph Street, Christchurch Central, Christchurch 8011<br>Subject: Arts, crafts and hobbies, Earthquake relief, Community groups, City planning, Community organization, Urban beautification, Earthquakes, Personal development<br>Last update: 12/5/2018<br>X latitude: -43.5363663<br>Y longitude: 172.6373873]]></description>
