    <Placemark>
      <name>Literacy Christchurch</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: Literacy Christchurch, begun in 1977, provides free basic literacy assistance for self-motivated adults, one-to-one or in groups, with reading, spelling, writing, numeracy, learner licence, Kiwi English, work readiness, workplace literacy. Tutoring is by trained tutors. Free training of volunteers leading to the National Certificate in Adult Literacy & Numeracy Education (NCALNE). Liaison with other literacy providers in the Canterbury area. Workplace literacy is also tutored<br>Contact person: Robyn Chandler<br>phone number: 366-9479<br>email: info@literacychristchurch.org.nz<br>website (or Fb): http://www.facebook.com/search/top/?q=literacy%20christchurch  http://www.aras.org.nz/<br>Address: 81 Buchan Street, Sydenham, Christchurch 8023<br>Subject: Community groups, Educational groups, Books and reading, Literacy programmes, Reading disability, Spelling ability, Languages, English language, Mathematics<br>Last update: 12/6/2018<br>X latitude: -43.5431032<br>Y longitude: 172.6380839]]></description>
