    <Placemark>
      <name>City Harvest Food Rescue Canterbury</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: City Harvest is a Christchurch-based independent, secular not-for-profit organisation that acts as a link between the food industry and the great community organisations that support people in need. City Harvest collaborates with food retailers and producers to rescue quality surplus food. This food is then provided to community groups that work directly with individuals and families who are struggling to make ends meet. <br>Contact person: Dr John Milligan<br>phone number: 930-1065<br>email: info@cityharvestnz.org<br>website (or Fb):  http://www.cityharvestnz.org  http://facebook.com/cityharvestnz/<br>Address: 352 Manchester Street, Christchurch central, Christchurch 8013<br>Subject: Citizen and consumer, Nonproft organizations, Volunteers, Community groups, Charities, Food security, Food supply, Hunger -- Prevention<br>Last update: 11/27/2018<br>X latitude: -43.521648<br>Y longitude: 172.6397929]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Description">
          <value>City Harvest is a Christchurch-based independent, secular not-for-profit organisation that acts as a link between the food industry and the great community organisations that support people in need. City Harvest collaborates with food retailers and producers to rescue quality surplus food. This food is then provided to community groups that work directly with individuals and families who are struggling to make ends meet. </value>
        </Data>
        <Data name="Contact person">
          <value>Dr John Milligan</value>
        </Data>
