    <Placemark>
      <name>Westminster Sports</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: WSI combines the interests of a number of sports clubs and community based organisations clustered around Christchurch/Westminster Park on Westminster Street, Mairehau. The clubs and organisations that currently form the membership of WSI cover eight different codes. In total 2,600 people are members of constituent clubs. WSI was formed to forge a progressive new direction for the administration, delivery of sports services, programmes and development of sport facilities/spaces in the Westminster catchment. Primarily serving the suburbs of Papanui, Redwood, Merivale, Shirley, St Albans, Marshlands and Mairehau while also recognising that many from a more widespread area will also benefit from our programmes and services. WSI is an Incorporated Society and is governed by a volunteer board. It currently has one full time employee<br>Contact person: Eddie Cropley<br>phone number: 385-1984<br>email: westsports@xtra.co.nz <br>website (or Fb): http://www.westminstersports.co.nz<br>Address: 250 Westminster Street, Mairehau, Christchurch 8013<br>Subject: Halls, meeting rooms, etc., Community groups, Sports and recreation, Australian football, Korfball, Lacrosse, Netball, Rugby Union football, Soccer, Squash (Game), Judo, Rugby Union football for children, Sports for women, Rugby Union football for women<br>Last update: 1/10/2019<br>X latitude: -43.5029115<br>Y longitude: 172.6461962]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Description">
          <value>WSI combines the interests of a number of sports clubs and community based organisations clustered around Christchurch/Westminster Park on Westminster Street, Mairehau. The clubs and organisations that currently form the membership of WSI cover eight different codes. In total 2,600 people are members of constituent clubs. WSI was formed to forge a progressive new direction for the administration, delivery of sports services, programmes and development of sport facilities/spaces in the Westminster catchment. Primarily serving the suburbs of Papanui, Redwood, Merivale, Shirley, St Albans, Marshlands and Mairehau while also recognising that many from a more widespread area will also benefit from our programmes and services. WSI is an Incorporated Society and is governed by a volunteer board. It currently has one full time employee</value>
        </Data>
