      <name>Te Whare Roimata Trust</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: For residents of the inner-city East area: Linwood Avenue to Madras Street to Cashel Street to Kilmore Street. Community centre; creche; support and out reach service; courses (parenting skills, self-esteem); ESOL evening for refugees and migrants with homework class for their children; sewing group for refugees and migrants; community garden (180 Smith St, open Monday - Friday, 9.00am -  3.00pm - ring first); and Linwood Community Arts Centre (corner Stanmore Road and Worcester Street) low cost art related activities including workshops, classes, concerts, performances and gallery space to rent<br>Contact person: Jenny Smith<br>phone number: 03-379 5134<br>email: TeWhareRoimata@clear.net.nz  <br>website (or Fb): <br>Address: 274 Gloucester Street, Christchurch Central, Christchurch 8011<br>Subject: Gardening, Community gardens, Organic gardening, Drop-in centres, Halls, meeting rooms, etc., Community groups, Ethnic groups, Social groups, Labour supply, Women -- Societies and clubs, Songs, Maori, Continuing education, Play groups, Hauora, Homelessness, Homeless persons -- Food, Homeless persons -- Services for, Welfare, Maori -- Services for, Reo MaÌ„ori<br>Last update: 1/9/2019<br>X latitude: -43.5303448<br>Y longitude: 172.6464693]]></description>
