    <Placemark>
      <name><![CDATA[Shakti Ethnic Women's Support Group Christchurch]]></name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: To facilitate an empowering environment for ethnic women so that they can bring about individual and social change. We provide the following services: emergency accommodation for women refugees, migrants or asylum seekers(and their children), life skills education programmes such as road safety, road code and finding employment workshops and seminars; information and advocacy for women and children who experience domestic violence; advocacy on behalf of ethnic women with government agencies, etc.; interpreters and language assistance in different languages; a drop-in centre for ethnic migrant and refugee women and children<br>Contact person: Carol Zhang<br>phone number: 0800-742-584, 389-2028<br>email: sewsg@shakti.org.nz<br>website (or Fb): http://www.shakti.org.nz<br>Address: 275-285 Hereford Street, Christchurch Central, Christchurch 8011<br>Subject: Citizen and consumer, Drop-in centres, Community groups, Ethnic groups, Women -- Societies and clubs, Homelessness, Homeless persons -- Housing, Homeless persons -- Services for, Shelters for the homeless, Victims -- Services for, Translating services, Life skills, Immigrants -- Services for, Refugees -- Services for<br>Last update: 1/8/2019<br>X latitude: -43.5319065<br>Y longitude: 172.6473796]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Description">
          <value>To facilitate an empowering environment for ethnic women so that they can bring about individual and social change. We provide the following services: emergency accommodation for women refugees, migrants or asylum seekers(and their children), life skills education programmes such as road safety, road code and finding employment workshops and seminars; information and advocacy for women and children who experience domestic violence; advocacy on behalf of ethnic women with government agencies, etc.; interpreters and language assistance in different languages; a drop-in centre for ethnic migrant and refugee women and children</value>
        </Data>
