          <value><![CDATA[YCD provides a unique inner city environment for young people to explore their talents and aspirations.  Whakatu-tia Nga Wero project, a service for young people with a history of offending between 12-16 years to gain skills to reduce the likelihood of reoffending, referred through Youth Justice;  Experienced youth workers are available  to support change and help young people to focus on develop their strengths. Community service hours' co-ordination through CY & F, Youth Justice Advocacy and Police. Case management, Supported bail. Street Work Project with young people under 18 who are sex workers (or at risk of becoming). Staff work on the streets 2 nights a week and run a drop-in service. Home visits (where appropriate), case management with a 'harm minimisation' focus and promotion of sexual health. Whanau Project is support parents and other members to understand and manage difficult behaviours.]]></value>
