    <Placemark>
      <name>Te Arawa Waka ki Otautahi</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: Te Arawa Waka ki Otautahi is a long-established taurahere ropu operating from Christchurch and serving the people of Canterbury. We call together nga uri na Te Arawa Waka to come together and learn the arts and crafts which their tupuna bestowed on them. With the aid of tikanga and kawa supported by waiata and korero, we tautoko the interests of things Maori in Christchurch and the wider South Island. We have a special focus on encouraging rangatahi to be involved in learning of and about all aspects of their whakapapa and taha Maori. First timers of any age are encouraged<br>Contact person: Eru Waiti<br>phone number: 383-5063<br>email: j.e.waiti@snap.net.nz<br>website (or Fb): <br>Address: 103 Metehau Street, Marshland, Christchurch 8083<br>Subject: Community groups, Ethnic groups, Maori -- Societies, etc., Whakapapa, Cultural groups<br>Last update: 1/9/2019<br>X latitude: -43.465764<br>Y longitude: 172.66408]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Description">
          <value>Te Arawa Waka ki Otautahi is a long-established taurahere ropu operating from Christchurch and serving the people of Canterbury. We call together nga uri na Te Arawa Waka to come together and learn the arts and crafts which their tupuna bestowed on them. With the aid of tikanga and kawa supported by waiata and korero, we tautoko the interests of things Maori in Christchurch and the wider South Island. We have a special focus on encouraging rangatahi to be involved in learning of and about all aspects of their whakapapa and taha Maori. First timers of any age are encouraged</value>
