    <Placemark>
      <name><![CDATA[Hillsborough/Heathcote Women's Institute]]></name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: Helping Glenelg Children's Camp, Cholmondeley Children's Home, and Women's Refuge; entertaining the elderly. We are women who meet once a month to discuss matters of interest to us all. It is non-sectarian and non-party political, and members meet on an equal footing. We ask every member to take her share of the responsibility in the conduct of the Institute. The Institute spirit means giving as well as getting, helping as well as being helped, if you know a good thing pass it on<br>Contact person: Glenda Sutherland<br>phone number: 338-0368<br>email: <br>website (or Fb): http://www.cwi.org.nz/<br>Address: St Marks Church Hall, Cnr. Opawa Road & Vincent Place, Christchurch 8023<br>Subject: Community groups, Women -- Societies and clubs, New Zealand Federation of Women's Institutes, New Zealand Federation of Women's Institutes<br>Last update: 11/29/2018<br>X latitude: -43.5524562<br>Y longitude: 172.6651431]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Description">
          <value><![CDATA[Helping Glenelg Children's Camp, Cholmondeley Children's Home, and Women's Refuge; entertaining the elderly. We are women who meet once a month to discuss matters of interest to us all. It is non-sectarian and non-party political, and members meet on an equal footing. We ask every member to take her share of the responsibility in the conduct of the Institute. The Institute spirit means giving as well as getting, helping as well as being helped, if you know a good thing pass it on]]></value>
