    <Placemark>
      <name>Christchurch Diamond Way Buddhist Centre</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: Diamond Way Buddhism New Zealand is part of an international network of 650 meditation centres in more than 50 countries around the world in the Karma Kagyu tradition of Tibetan Buddhism. The centres were founded by Lama Ole Nydahl according to the wishes of the 16th Karmapa. They are now under the guidance of the 17th Gyalwa Karmapa, Trinley Thaye Dorje<br>Contact person: Niki Jimenez<br>phone number: 381-3108<br>email: christchurch@buddhism.org.nz<br>website (or Fb): http://www.facebook.com/DiamondWayBuddhismChristchurch http://www.buddhism.org.nz<br>Address: 220 England Street, Linwood,  Christchurch 8011<br>Subject: Community groups, Buddhism, Trusts and trustees<br>Last update: 11/21/2018<br>X latitude: -43.525902<br>Y longitude: 172.6665831]]></description>
