    <Placemark>
      <name>Bromley Community Centre</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: Bromley Community Centre is a wahi huihuinga, or gathering place. It is a community hub that offers a range of programmes, activities and events that are actively promoted and provided to members of the local community. Our vision is to establish, develop, and administer community facilities in Bromley and surrounding areas, to foster the growth of community spirit, and to encourage local people to participate in social, recreational, educational, cultural, and other such activities. Currently, Katang Fitness (4 times per week), Womenâ€™s Group, Playgroup, Computer Tuition, Afterschool Childrenâ€™s Recreation, Yoga, and Art Group are offered as the Centreâ€™s weekly programmes and also a School Holiday Programme. The Centre also holds events and works collaboratively with other local organisations to be able to offer a wider range of community events. The events include Bromley Fair, Market Days, Matariki Event, Repair Cafe and more. We have groups that hire our facility and run programmes such as Line Dancing, Affordable Fruit and Vege Group (Packing and Distribution Centre), Zuu Fitness and Home School Drama.<br>Contact person: Hana Kakoi<br>phone number: 389-1657<br>email: bromleyccentre@gmail.com<br>website (or Fb): http://www.facebook.com/bromley.communitycentre<br>Address: 45 Bromley Road, Bromley,  Christchurch 8062<br>Subject: Community centres, Drop-in centres, Halls, meeting rooms, etc., Community groups, Youth -- Societies and clubs, Youth -- Services for, Cultural groups, Dance, Line dancing, Play groups, Health and welfare, Health, Homelessness, Homeless persons -- Services for, Physical fitness, Parenting, Home and family, Food, Personal development, Computers, Karate, Physical fitness, Exercise, Scrapbooking<br>Last update: 11/13/2018<br>X latitude: -43.5383143<br>Y longitude: 172.6916547]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Description">
          <value>Bromley Community Centre is a wahi huihuinga, or gathering place. It is a community hub that offers a range of programmes, activities and events that are actively promoted and provided to members of the local community. Our vision is to establish, develop, and administer community facilities in Bromley and surrounding areas, to foster the growth of community spirit, and to encourage local people to participate in social, recreational, educational, cultural, and other such activities. Currently, Katang Fitness (4 times per week), Womenâ€™s Group, Playgroup, Computer Tuition, Afterschool Childrenâ€™s Recreation, Yoga, and Art Group are offered as the Centreâ€™s weekly programmes and also a School Holiday Programme. The Centre also holds events and works collaboratively with other local organisations to be able to offer a wider range of community events. The events include Bromley Fair, Market Days, Matariki Event, Repair Cafe and more. We have groups that hire our facility and run programmes such as Line Dancing, Affordable Fruit and Vege Group (Packing and Distribution Centre), Zuu Fitness and Home School Drama.</value>
