    <Placemark>
      <name>New Brighton Pier and Foreshore Society</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: The New Brighton Pier and Foreshore Society was formed in 1964. Since then it has worked and continues to work on the enhancement and promotion of the wider New Brighton foreshore and surrounds communities. Most 'famous' for the work surrounding the fundraising and coordination of the rebuild of the New Brighton Pier, the organisation is currently working on promoting and fundraising for the CCC Legacy Project - the Hot Salt Water Pools.<br>Contact person: <br>phone number: 021-330-714<br>email: pierforeshore@gmail.com<br>website (or Fb): <br>Address: Board Room, New Brighton Working-men's Club, 202 Marine Parade, Christchurch, 8083<br>Subject: Citizen and consumer, Conservation of natural resources, Community groups<br>Last update: 12/13/2018<br>X latitude: -43.5056643<br>Y longitude: 172.7301316]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Description">
          <value><![CDATA[The New Brighton Pier and Foreshore Society was formed in 1964. Since then it has worked and continues to work on the enhancement and promotion of the wider New Brighton foreshore and surrounds communities. Most 'famous' for the work surrounding the fundraising and coordination of the rebuild of the New Brighton Pier, the organisation is currently working on promoting and fundraising for the CCC Legacy Project - the Hot Salt Water Pools.]]></value>
        </Data>
