    <Placemark>
      <name>Al-Huda Islamic Charitable Trust</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: To maintain the cultural identity of our extended community as an enriching dimension, while bridging with the New Zealand culture by emphasis on similarities for better adhering and integration within the New Zealand Society.  To provide out-of-school care in form of social, sporting and educational activities to the attendees with a get-together space, competitive social activities plus teaching Arabic which was provided indiscriminately to Arabs and non-Arabs. We always extend an open invitation to anyone who would be interested to join our activities or study Arabic. To provide for sound bi-cultural youngsters who will promote and facilitate trade and cultural ties with the Middle East in near future, where these ties are progressing ahead with New Zealand opening up new embassies in Egypt and others. Also recent trends show New Zealand becoming a premier destination for graduate and post-graduate academic studies for students from the Middle East, which will require better understanding and promotion. Please visit our website below for more details<br>Contact person: Baher Zaghlool<br>phone number: 021-399-277<br>email: <br>website (or Fb): <br>Address: Rooms E5-E7, Block E. Hagley Community College, 510 Hagley Avenue, Christchurch, 8011<br>Subject: Community groups, Islam, Trusts and trustees, Ethnic groups, Muslims, Health and welfare, After-school programmes, Arabic language<br>Last update: 10/31/2018<br>X latitude: -43.5379366<br>Y longitude: 172.6236309]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Description">
          <value>To maintain the cultural identity of our extended community as an enriching dimension, while bridging with the New Zealand culture by emphasis on similarities for better adhering and integration within the New Zealand Society.  To provide out-of-school care in form of social, sporting and educational activities to the attendees with a get-together space, competitive social activities plus teaching Arabic which was provided indiscriminately to Arabs and non-Arabs. We always extend an open invitation to anyone who would be interested to join our activities or study Arabic. To provide for sound bi-cultural youngsters who will promote and facilitate trade and cultural ties with the Middle East in near future, where these ties are progressing ahead with New Zealand opening up new embassies in Egypt and others. Also recent trends show New Zealand becoming a premier destination for graduate and post-graduate academic studies for students from the Middle East, which will require better understanding and promotion. Please visit our website below for more details</value>
        </Data>
        <Data name="Contact person">
          <value>Baher Zaghlool</value>
        </Data>
        <Data name="phone number">
          <value>021-399-277</value>
        </Data>
