    <Placemark>
      <name>Angel Fund Wahine Putea</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: A step ahead loan fund lending up to $500 interest-free to women on low incomes who live in the Christchurch area who have difficulty accessing credit from traditional sources and who have an ability to repay. The loan purpose must meet one of the following; training and/or further education, transition to work expenses, pre-commercial business proposals, emergencies that are preventing transition to work or education. Angel Fund also offers a saving scheme<br>Contact person: Fran<br>phone number: 022-412-6435<br>email: angelfund@gmail.com<br>website (or Fb): http://www.angelfund.org.nz<br>Address: 399 Cashel Street, Linwood, Christchurch 8011<br>Subject: Community groups, Health and welfare, Homelessness, Homeless women -- Finance, Personal, Loans, Personal, Women -- Finance, Personal, Women -- Employment re-entry, Personal development<br>Last update: 10/31/2018<br>X latitude: -43.532718<br>Y longitude: 172.6545312]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Description">
          <value>A step ahead loan fund lending up to $500 interest-free to women on low incomes who live in the Christchurch area who have difficulty accessing credit from traditional sources and who have an ability to repay. The loan purpose must meet one of the following; training and/or further education, transition to work expenses, pre-commercial business proposals, emergencies that are preventing transition to work or education. Angel Fund also offers a saving scheme</value>
