      <name>Akaroa Heartland Services and Resource Centre</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: Akaroa Heartlands provides a one-stop shop for government and community services and information.  Heartlands provides a community hub for local people to discuss their needs directly with government agencies and community organisations.  We provide a friendly face to face confidential service offering support, advocacy, resources and information <br>Contact person: Kerry Little<br>phone number: 03 304-8659,03 304-8659<br>email: heartlands.coordinator@gmail.com<br>website (or Fb): http://www.heartlandservices.govt.nz/locations/akaroa.html<br>Address: 39 Rue Lavaud Akaroa 7520<br>Subject: Citizen and consumer, Conservation of natural resources, Halls, meeting rooms, etc., Meals on wheels programmes, Community groups, Job creation, Health and welfare, Home and family<br>Last update: 10/31/2018<br>X latitude: -43.8033076<br>Y longitude: 172.96861149999995]]></description>
