    <Placemark>
      <name>Akaroa Heritage Park Trust</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Description: The Objects of the Trust under its constitution are to develop and maintain Tree Parks in Akaroa for the benefit of the public; to make the parks accessible to the public by developing walkways to and in the parks; to promote education about the planting and preservation of trees;  to encourage the planting and preservation of trees in New Zealand and  in particular Akaroa and the Banks Peninsula. <br>Contact person: Virginia Wigram<br>phone number: 03 304-8556<br>email: <br>website (or Fb): https://akaroa.com/sporting-recreation/akaroa-heritage-park<br>Address: Long Bay Road, Akaroa<br>Subject: Conservation of natural resources, Community groups, Trusts and trustees, Tree planting<br>Last update: 10/31/2018<br>X latitude: -43.8013206<br>Y longitude: 173.0048071]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Description">
          <value>The Objects of the Trust under its constitution are to develop and maintain Tree Parks in Akaroa for the benefit of the public; to make the parks accessible to the public by developing walkways to and in the parks; to promote education about the planting and preservation of trees;  to encourage the planting and preservation of trees in New Zealand and  in particular Akaroa and the Banks Peninsula. </value>
